-- EXPECT-ERROR: `Cap(IO)` cannot be deserialized
-- Capability unforgeability (R3), derive over a variant argument (2026-08-05).
--
-- `derive Json for T` generates a decoder for every constructor argument.
-- `encoder_for_ty` / `decode_value_at` in lib/desugar/desugar.ml:1585+ fall
-- back to "assume the nested type also derives Json" for any type they do not
-- recognise, and `Cap(IO)` is not recognised — so before this check the codec
-- was generated over the capability position without objection, and the
-- decoder ran far enough to return a Json.DecodeError rather than refusing to
-- exist at all.
--
-- `needs IO` keeps the needs-coverage checks silent so this file isolates
-- Check A. Companion: reject/t145 is the record-field spelling of the same
-- hole; accept/t143 is a cap-free derive in a cap-using module.
mod DeriveVariantForge do
  needs IO

  type Loot = Loot(Cap(IO))
  derive Json for Loot

  fn main() do
    println("codec generated over a capability position")
  end
end
